I have my boxes in my old room.
Nina helps me.
We carry the boxes over to my new apartment.
I do not have many things.
It is just my clothes and my books.
But two of the boxes are heavy.
Nina asks.
"What is in this box?"
"It is my books," I answer.
We walk down the hall.
We carry the boxes into my apartment.
We put them on the floor.
Now there are four boxes standing by the door.
"Welcome, neighbor!" laughs Nina.
"Thank you very much for the help," I say.
She goes into her own apartment again.
